email.task:
You are an IT support technician. Kevin, an accountant, reported that his desktop computer makes a loud noise and sometimes switches itself off. Write an email to Kevin explaining what you have already done and what he can do now, using the notes below. In your email you must use:
- the present perfect with already and with yet (I have already…, I haven't… yet);
- may, might or could to talk about a possible cause;
- should or try + -ing to suggest a solution.
Follow the standard layout for an email giving instructions: From / To / Date / Subject, a greeting, It should be quite easy to …, the steps with First / Then / Next / After that / Finally, a reminder (Don't forget to … when you've finished.), then Best wishes and your name, position and department.
Write 80–100 words (do not count the From, To, Date and Subject lines).
